pper rule (absolute offset not printed). Sensitivity is the reciprocal of the exposure (J/cm2) required to produce a specified density, which the sheet gives as 1.0 above D-min. Besides b/g/r the plot has the dashed light-blue curve of the cyan-sensitive fourth layer, traced as line l4 (build.py ignores it). Each layer curve ends in near-vertical drops, so the last few nm are approximated on the 5 nm grid.","Spectral dye density plot has only 'mid' (Mid-scale Density, a neutral mid-scale subject) and 'min' (Minimum Density), no separate c/m/y dyes; the curves run 400-720 nm.","Grain: diffuse RMS granularity 7 (heading 15, printed '..............7'); micro-densitometer aperture 48 um, magnification 12x, sample density 1.0 above minimum density. Film speed ISO 1600/33 deg daylight (tungsten 3200 K: ISO 400 with LBB-12). No paper is recommended on the sheet. Grey card read through the red filter should give 0.65-0.85 (Status M), not used here."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":28.0,"grain_size":44.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}